{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And he took six hundred chariots.</b> Rashi, of blessed memory, wrote: From whom were they? If you say from Pharaoh's own — was it not already said (Exodus 9:3), ״הנה יד ה' הויה במקנה אשר בשדה״? And if you say from Israel's own — was it not already said (Exodus 10:26), ״וגם מקננו ילך עמנו לא תשאר פרסה״? From whom were they? From those who feared the word of HaShem among the Egyptians — from this came benefit to Israel. Hence the Sages, of blessed memory, interpreted in Masekhet Soferim: Rabbi Shimon bar Yohai said: The best of the Egyptians — kill him in time of war; and the best of serpents — crush his brain. And they derived it from this verse. The explanation of the matter is that only in time of war is it permitted to kill him, for since he fights against you and comes against you to kill you, you too must rise early to kill him. Not in time of war it is forbidden, for behold even in time of war we were commanded to offer them peace, and even for the seven nations concerning whom it is written (Deuteronomy 20:16), ״לא תחיה כל נשמה״. But when he comes against the Holy One, blessed be He — that is, he intends to rebel against Him, in the manner of the Egyptians — even not in time of war it is permitted, because it is a war for HaShem. For since the Egyptians already saw in the plague of the firstborn that the Holy One, blessed be He, Himself in His glory was the one striking, and now they return to the sea — their intention was none other than to wage war against the Holy One, blessed be He. Therefore Moses said to them, ״HaShem will fight for you״ — that is, since they still pursue you, from now on the war is for the Name, blessed be He, and therefore they deserved to be drowned in the sea." "<b>And thirty over all of it.</b> As its Targum renders: וגברין ממנן על כלהון — 'and men appointed over all of them' — that is, he appointed officers of hundreds and officers of thousands to be appointed over all that mighty host and to lead them. Or one may say, ושלשים על כלו — that all that host was divided into three companies, and therefore we find that they perished in the sea in three companies, as it is written, ״לכל חיל פרעה הבאים אחריהם בים״, and it is written, ״מרכבות פרעה וחילו ירה בים״, and it is written, ״כי בא סוס פרעה ברכבו ובפרשיו בים״."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:58:52.964553347Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}